The first foreign environment should remain deliberately small.

Target scope:

FOREIGN SERVER

├── TERMINAL
├── FILES
└── SYSTEM

Do not recreate every NODE-OS application.

Do not add:

- Wallet
- Notes
- Scan
- Processes
- Tools launcher
- Home widgets
- NODE-OS launcher
- NODE-OS status bars copied verbatim

unless an actual accepted requirement discovered after Work Order 04 makes one
of those necessary.

This operating surface exists to prove that a remote Device can expose its own
canonical state through its own Firmware.


6. REMOTE TERMINAL

Add the first Terminal belonging to the foreign Device operating surface.

This is NOT a retargeting of the existing NODE-OS Terminal.

The local NODE-OS Terminal continues to operate the local Device exactly as
before.

The foreign Terminal receives its own narrow remote operating context derived
from the active RemoteSession.

V1 remote Terminal should provide only the commands needed to prove the remote
context.

A likely minimal set is:

help
clear
ip
status
ls
cat
disconnect

Adapt this list against accepted main and the approved server-Firmware design.

Do not automatically copy every NODE-OS Terminal command.

Do not expose:

- analyze
- attack
- scan
- remote Process execution
- generic arbitrary command execution

solely because those commands exist in NODE-OS.


7. PROVE LOCAL AND REMOTE TERMINALS ARE DIFFERENT CONTEXTS

This is a critical acceptance boundary.

While connected:

NODE-OS Terminal:

ip
status
ls
cat

must continue to observe the local Device.

Foreign Terminal:

ip
status
ls
cat

must observe the foreign Device state appropriate to that command.

There must be no implicit global command retargeting.

Conceptually:

NODE-OS TERMINAL
ls
    ↓
node-01.filesystem

FOREIGN TERMINAL
ls
    ↓
srv-01.filesystem

The context chooses the Device.

The command verb does not.


8. ADD THE FIRST CANONICAL REMOTE FILESYSTEM

Use the neutral FilesystemState / TextFile model established in Work Order 03.

The first operable foreign server may now own its own canonical filesystem.

Do not create a second remote-only filesystem model.

Do not store remote files in:

- React state
- the remote Files component
- the remote Terminal
- RemoteSession
- DeviceAccess

Files belong to the remote Device.


INITIAL FOREIGN FILESYSTEM

Keep V1 intentionally small.

Add only enough neutral content to prove that the remote filesystem is a
different canonical filesystem from node-01.

Do not introduce gameplay secrets yet.

Do not add:

- credentials
- passwords
- SSH keys
- exploit hints
- vulnerability clues
- logs
- malware
- auth history
- network intelligence
