12. SESSION AUTHORITY PRESENTATION

The foreign operating surface may present the authority under which the active
Session operates.

That authority must derive through:

RemoteSession
    ↓
DeviceAccess
    ↓
canonical privilege

Do not duplicate privilege into Firmware state.

Do not create a user-account framework.

For the first current access route, the expected represented authority remains
the concrete privilege established by DeviceAccess.


13. DISCONNECT FROM THE FOREIGN SURFACE

The foreign operating surface must provide an explicit DISCONNECT path.

It must invoke the same shared disconnect operation introduced in Work Order 04.

Do not create a foreign-UI-only connection state.

On disconnect:

- RemoteSession is cleared
- foreign operating surface closes
- NODE-OS becomes the active local presentation again
- DeviceAccess remains
- remote filesystem remains
- Discovery remains
- Knowledge remains
- local filesystem remains
- all unrelated canonical state remains

Do not require another Attack to reconnect.


14. DO NOT CHANGE EXISTING NODE-OS COMMAND SEMANTICS

The introduction of a foreign Terminal must not mutate the semantics of the
existing local Terminal.

In particular, the existence of an active RemoteSession must not cause local:

ip
status
ls
cat

to operate remotely.

If existing NODE-OS command context has to be refactored to support clean reuse,
keep the context narrow and preserve all existing behavior.

Do not give either Terminal unrestricted GameState access merely because there
are now two contexts.


15. DO NOT IMPLEMENT REMOTE PROCESS EXECUTION YET

The foreign server may be operable without yet becoming a Process executor.

Do not in this milestone:

- start Processes on the remote Device
- assign remote CPU capacity
- assign remote RAM capacity
- move existing Processes to the remote Device
- implement distributed execution
- implement malware execution
- implement background services as Processes

Remote Process execution should become a concrete later mechanic only after
remote compute requirements are defined.


16. DO NOT IMPLEMENT FIREWALL OR REACHABILITY YET

The purpose of Prompt 05 is to make the first RemoteSession visibly and
functionally meaningful.

It does not yet make network position strategically different.

Do not introduce:

- Firewall rules
- Reachability rules
- routes
- pivots
- internal-only targets
- gateway state
- tunnels
- network-path simulation
- second-hop observation rules

The next planned gameplay milestone will use the foreign Device / Session as one
